      "documentConcept": "PD diagnosis criteria and differential diagnosis",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:c4de134d106937fb60191ba1ba46262c48f19e15aadfc6a8d0845f3c99d3f52a",
      "text": "PD diagnosis requires distinguishing motor parkinsonism from its cause. The 2015 MDS criteria combine a mandatory motor syndrome with absolute exclusions, supportive findings and timed red flags, with separate clinically established and clinically probable categories. Specialist history, examination, medication review and reassessment help distinguish PD from essential tremor, drug-induced and vascular parkinsonism, normal-pressure hydrocephalus, functional presentations and atypical neurodegenerative syndromes. Published validation against expert diagnosis should be distinguished from pathological confirmation; autopsy series show clinical overlap and limitations of retrospective documentation.",
